    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="1141" n="1007" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg1007"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/7–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 676 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of African Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Villard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d676-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-13T21:00:00+02:00">July 13, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4225. From Villard.</p>
                <p>… With reference London’s 6984 July 11 to Dept,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d676-f2"/>
                    Peake reaffirms intention of British government not to raise at Berlin any
                    question concerning extent of Russian participation which is accepted in
                    principle role [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] subject of any discussion
                    concerning Tangier between British and Russians being envisaged as limited to
                    deal by which British would obtain something in exchange for Russian admission
                    to conversations. British believe French will accept postponement of
                    conversations until first week August.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d676-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d676-f1-content">
                <p>Sent over the signature of Caffery. The gist of this message was included in
                    telegram No. 35 of July 16 from Grew to Byrnes (file No. 800.00
                    Summaries/7–1645).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d676-f2" n="2" xml:id="d676-f2-content">
